DOM XSS via client-side prototype pollution
Information
Category: Prototype Pollution
Difficulty: Practitioner
Status: ✅ Solved
Author: Alejandro Jiménez
Objective

Exploit a client-side prototype pollution vulnerability to achieve DOM-based Cross-Site Scripting (DOM XSS).

The application allows an attacker to modify Object.prototype through parameters in the URL. A vulnerable JavaScript gadget subsequently reads a property from an object and incorporates it into an eval() call.

The exploitation chain is:

Prototype Pollution
        ↓
Object.prototype.sequence
        ↓
manager.sequence
        ↓
eval()
        ↓
JavaScript execution
        ↓
alert(1)
