Conclusion

This lab demonstrates how client-side prototype pollution can be chained with an existing JavaScript gadget to achieve DOM XSS.

The prototype pollution itself does not execute JavaScript. The critical component is the vulnerable gadget:

manager.sequence

which is subsequently incorporated into:

eval()

The final payload:

/?__proto__.sequence=alert(1)-

bypasses the numeric character appended by the application and produces valid JavaScript.

The complete attack therefore consists of:

Prototype Pollution
        +
Gadget
        +
eval()
        =
DOM XSS

The lab was successfully solved when the injected alert(1) executed in the browser.
